\begin_layout Standard
One concern with this strategy is that,
 because bargaining begins from the randomly assigned offer price,
 that price may anchor the elicited WTP,
 so that the WTP measure used to identify screening would partly reflect the random anchor rather than farmers' true valuations.
 In our data,
 the offer does anchor stated valuations:
 a one-shilling increase in the initial offer raises elicited WTP by 
