 A joint test that regresses the discount assignment on all covariates in Table 1 does not reject orthogonality (F(11,693)=1.33,
 p=0.21).
 Balance also holds for the second,
 individual-level randomization of the initial offer price:
 none of the covariates in Table 1 predicts the offer price at the 5 percent level,
 and the corresponding joint test does not reject orthogonality either (F(11,693)=1.51,
 p=0.13).
