Appendix:
 Anchoring of the Initial Offer Price
\begin_inset CommandInset label
LatexCommand label
name "sec:Appendix-C:-Anchoring"

\end_inset


\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
This appendix reports the estimates underlying the anchoring discussion in the estimation section.
 Regressing elicited willingness to pay on the randomized initial offer yields a coefficient of 
\begin_inset ERT
status open

\begin_layout Plain Layout

\backslash
Sexpr{anchor$wtp_coef}
\end_layout

\end_inset

 (
\begin_inset ERT
status open

\begin_layout Plain Layout
$
\backslash
Sexpr{anchor$wtp_pmath}$
\end_layout

\end_inset

),
 confirming that the offer anchors stated valuations,
 though by only about 
\begin_inset ERT
status open

\begin_layout Plain Layout

\backslash
Sexpr{anchor$pass_pct}
\end_layout

\end_inset

% of mean willingness to pay across the offer range.
 The initial offer is orthogonal to the randomized discount:
 regressing the offer on the sunk-cost (paid-versus-free) indicator gives a coefficient of 
\begin_inset ERT
status open

\begin_layout Plain Layout

\backslash
Sexpr{anchor$bal_coef}
\end_layout

\end_inset

 shillings (
\begin_inset ERT
status open

\begin_layout Plain Layout
$
\backslash
Sexpr{anchor$bal_pmath}$
\end_layout

\end_inset

),
 and the offer does not interact with the discount in the sunk-cost regressions (
\begin_inset ERT
status open

\begin_layout Plain Layout
$
\backslash
Sexpr{anchor$sunkint_pmath}$
\end_layout

\end_inset

).
 Finally,
 the screening coefficient is insensitive to the anchor:
 for the trial-seed use index,
 the willingness-to-pay coefficient is 
\begin_inset ERT
status open

\begin_layout Plain Layout

\backslash
Sexpr{anchor$scr_with}
\end_layout

\end_inset

 when the initial offer is included as a control and 
\begin_inset ERT
status open

\begin_layout Plain Layout

\backslash
Sexpr{anchor$scr_wout}
\end_layout

\end_inset

 when it is omitted.
\end_layout

