\begin_layout Standard
As a robustness check,
 we re-estimate all main specifications after excluding farmers whose willingness to pay was right-censored---that is,
 the 118 farmers whose negotiated price equals the randomly assigned initial offer (111 accepted the initial offer outright,
 while 7 returned to it after bargaining).
 For these farmers,
 the observed transaction price represents a lower bound on their true willingness to pay,
 potentially attenuating the screening estimates.
 Tables
\begin_inset space ~
\end_inset


\begin_inset CommandInset ref
LatexCommand ref
reference "tab:Effects-on-Use-nocens"

\end_inset

--
\begin_inset CommandInset ref
LatexCommand ref
reference "tab:Effects-on-Adoption-nocens"

\end_inset

 report the results.
 The main findings are qualitatively unchanged.
 Screening effects on trial seed use remain significant,
 and the pattern of null adoption and input use results combined with significant production effects in the subsequent season is confirmed.
 Some individual coefficients lose precision,
 as expected given the roughly 16 percent smaller sample,
 but point estimates are stable throughout.
